<Layouts.app flash={@flash} current_scope={@current_scope}>
  <div id="privacy-policy">
    <.legal_document
      draft={false}
      eyebrow={dgettext("legal", "Your information")}
      title={dgettext("legal", "Privacy policy")}
      description={
        dgettext(
          "legal",
          "This policy explains which personal information Gesttalt handles, why it is needed, how long it is kept, and the choices available to you."
        )
      }
    >
      <section data-part="section">
        <h2 data-part="title">{dgettext("legal", "Controller")}</h2>
        <dl data-part="facts">
          <dt>{dgettext("legal", "Name")}</dt><dd>Pedro Piñera Buendía</dd>
          <dt>{dgettext("legal", "Trading as")}</dt><dd>Gesttalt</dd>
          <dt>{dgettext("legal", "Email")}</dt><dd>
            <a href="mailto:gesttalt@pepicrft.me">gesttalt@pepicrft.me</a>
          </dd>
          <dt>{dgettext("legal", "Last updated")}</dt><dd>23 July 2026</dd>
        </dl>
        <p>
          No data protection officer has been appointed because Gesttalt is not currently required
          to appoint one.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section data-part="section">
        <h2 data-part="title">{dgettext("legal", "Information, purpose, and legal basis")}</h2>
        <dl data-part="facts">
          <dt>{dgettext("legal", "Account and authentication")}</dt><dd>
            Email address, password hash, login links, session records, and security events are
            used to create and secure your account and perform the service contract. The legal
            basis is Article 6(1)(b) of the General Data Protection Regulation.
          </dd>
          <dt>{dgettext("legal", "Publication")}</dt><dd>
            Posts, pages, images, themes, publication settings, domain names, and delivery records
            are processed to store and publish material at your direction. The legal basis is
            Article 6(1)(b) of the General Data Protection Regulation.
          </dd>
          <dt>{dgettext("legal", "Connected applications")}</dt><dd>
            Application details, authorization grants, public keys, and security tokens are
            processed to provide requested publishing interfaces and protect accounts. The legal
            bases are Article 6(1)(b) and Article 6(1)(f) of the General Data Protection Regulation.
            The legitimate interest is operating a secure, interoperable service.
          </dd>
          <dt>{dgettext("legal", "Service operation and security")}</dt><dd>
            Network address, request metadata, browser and transport signals, error logs, delivery
            logs, and aggregated service measurements are processed to prevent abuse, diagnose
            failures, and keep the service reliable. The legal basis is Article 6(1)(f) of the
            General Data Protection Regulation. The legitimate interests are service security and
            reliability.
          </dd>
          <dt>{dgettext("legal", "Messages and legal reports")}</dt><dd>
            Contact details, correspondence, reported content addresses, explanations, and
            decisions are processed to answer requests and comply with legal duties. The legal
            bases are Article 6(1)(c) and Article 6(1)(f) of the General Data Protection Regulation.
            The legitimate interests are resolving requests, protecting rights, and documenting
            responsible moderation.
          </dd>
        </dl>
      </section>

      <section data-part="section">
        <h2 data-part="title">{dgettext("legal", "Required information and sources")}</h2>
        <p>
          An email address is required to create an account because Gesttalt uses it to confirm
          ownership, authenticate you, and send security notices. Without it, an account cannot be
          provided. Publication and support information is supplied by you. Request and security
          information is generated when you use the service. Domain information may also be read
          from public Domain Name System records.
        </p>
        <p>
          Gesttalt does not use your information for advertising, sell it, or make decisions with
          legal or similarly significant effects solely by automated means. Illegal-content
          reports and moderation decisions are assessed by a person.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section data-part="section">
        <h2 data-part="title">
          {dgettext("legal", "Service providers and international transfers")}
        </h2>
        <dl data-part="facts">
          <dt>Hetzner Online GmbH</dt><dd>
            Provides computing, network delivery, database infrastructure, object storage, and
            backups in Germany. Gesttalt selects the Falkenstein, Germany region.
            <a href="https://www.hetzner.com/legal/privacy-policy/" rel="external">
              Hetzner privacy information
            </a>
          </dd>
          <dt>Cloudflare, Inc.</dt><dd>
            Provides Turnstile abuse protection on account registration and legal-reporting forms.
            It receives the network address and browser, transport, site, and challenge signals
            needed to distinguish people from automated abuse. Processing outside the European
            Economic Area may occur under Cloudflare's data-processing terms and applicable
            transfer safeguards.
            <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/" rel="external">
              Turnstile privacy information
            </a>
          </dd>
          <dt>Plunk</dt><dd>
            Delivers transactional email through Gesttalt's mail relay. Primary hosted processing
            is in Germany. Amazon Web Services Simple Email Service may transmit messages
            internationally under the European Commission's standard contractual clauses.
            <a href="https://www.useplunk.com/dpa" rel="external">
              Plunk data-processing terms
            </a>
          </dd>
          <dt>Fastmail Pty Ltd</dt><dd>
            Hosts the gesttalt@pepicrft.me mailbox used for support, privacy requests, and legal
            reports. Fastmail is based in Australia and uses the European Commission's standard
            contractual clauses for restricted transfers.
            <a href="https://www.fastmail.com/policies/dpa/" rel="external">
              Fastmail data-processing terms
            </a>
          </dd>
        </dl>
        <p>
          Gesttalt may disclose information to courts, regulators, law-enforcement authorities, or
          other recipients when legally required, or when necessary to establish, exercise, or
          defend legal claims.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section data-part="section">
        <h2 data-part="title">{dgettext("legal", "Retention")}</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Unconfirmed accounts are automatically deleted after 30 days.
          </li>
          <li>
            Active account and publication information is kept while the account exists. A
            permanent deletion job is available in <a href={~p"/users/settings"}>account settings</a>. It removes the account, publication,
            connected applications, and stored media; encrypted backups expire within 30 days.
          </li>
          <li>
            Login links are removed after 15 minutes, email-change links after 7 days, and browser
            session records after 14 days. Expired application authorization records are removed
            within 35 days. Expired or revoked agent registration records are removed after 7 days.
          </li>
          <li>
            Application request, error, and security logs are kept for 7 days. Service measurements
            are kept for 15 days.
          </li>
          <li>
            Resolved illegal-content reports and their decision records are automatically deleted
            after 3 years. Open reports are kept until a decision is completed.
          </li>
          <li>
            Support, privacy, and legal correspondence in the contact mailbox is deleted no later
            than 3 years after the matter closes, unless longer retention is required for a legal
            claim or by law.
          </li>
          <li>
            Plunk states that application programming interface logs and hosted backups are deleted
            after 30 days. Temporary mail relay queues retain a message only while delivery is
            attempted.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          A legal preservation duty or active claim may require a limited record to be kept longer.
          When that duty ends, the record is deleted.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section data-part="section">
        <h2 data-part="title">{dgettext("legal", "Cookies and browser storage")}</h2>
        <p>
          Gesttalt uses only storage necessary to provide requested features. The signed session
          cookie maintains a login for the current browser session. If “Keep me logged in” is
          selected, a signed authentication cookie lasts up to 14 days. Theme previews use session
          storage until the browser tab closes. Cloudflare Turnstile uses the signals and storage
          necessary to protect registration and reporting forms. No advertising or optional
          analytics storage is used.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section data-part="section">
        <h2 data-part="title">{dgettext("legal", "Your rights")}</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on the circumstances, you may request access, correction, deletion,
          restriction, or portability of your information, and you may object to processing based
          on legitimate interests. Where processing relies on consent, you may withdraw it for the
          future. Contact <a href="mailto:gesttalt@pepicrft.me">gesttalt@pepicrft.me</a>. Gesttalt may need to verify
          your identity before fulfilling a request.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may complain to any competent supervisory authority. The authority for the Berlin
          establishment is the Berlin Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information,
          Alt-Moabit 59-61, 10555 Berlin, Germany, <a href="mailto:mailbox@datenschutz-berlin.de">mailbox@datenschutz-berlin.de</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section data-part="section">
        <h2 data-part="title">{dgettext("legal", "Customer publications")}</h2>
        <p>
          A publication owner separately determines how information from its visitors is used and
          is responsible for its own legal notices and privacy information. When Gesttalt processes
          visitor information solely on a publication owner's instructions, the publication owner
          is the controller and Gesttalt is the processor. Contact
          <a href="mailto:gesttalt@pepicrft.me">gesttalt@pepicrft.me</a>
          before using Gesttalt for processing that requires a written data-processing agreement.
        </p>
      </section>
    </.legal_document>
  </div>
</Layouts.app>
